      "title": "Syrian reactor could have been used for nuclear weapons if completed, UN says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/syrian-reactor-could-nuclear-weapons-if-completed-un",
      "description": "<p>Chief of nuclear watchdog says secret Assad-era facility would have been able to produce fissile material </p><p>A nearly complete nuclear reactor built secretly during the rule of the toppled Syrian leader Bashar al-Assad would have been able to produce fissile material for possible use in nuclear weapons, the chief of the UN nuclear watchdog has revealed.</p><p>Inspectors from the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) last month visited two sites, one in Deir ez-Zor and a second in an undisclosed location identified to them by Syrian authorities.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/syrian-reactor-could-nuclear-weapons-if-completed-un\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T16:37:31"
    },
